#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a9c101-6040-5f1b-801d-2fbfe20bc200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383253} {:answer/id #uuid "63bf3027-e5e3-5155-a2ae-b3868a2b239d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383254} {:answer/id #uuid "c18299b4-08b7-5050-bdf0-67673df597ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383255} {:answer/id #uuid "44c339db-5776-5817-80dc-407ee9a16d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383256} {:answer/id #uuid "ab946482-d5f1-5b8b-afec-fe7af533a64c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63bf3027-e5e3-5155-a2ae-b3868a2b239d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383254} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a8dd7df-6ab1-5986-87a4-4cf5c94f9847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "780bb8b5-f350-5f18-b702-f18d3b60c284" :question/math-academy-id "q-129120" :question/problem "Given that $Q(5,-1,9)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,-2⟩=3$, find the shortest distance from $P(7,-2,8)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,9⟩-⟨7,-2,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨3,-6,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6-6-2|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-14|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077d3150-975a-51a9-9216-1a486213b1d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383267} {:answer/id #uuid "daf22698-4613-5982-8786-c0d5ba6cad6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383268} {:answer/id #uuid "c801d42b-7f0d-5c60-b475-a966bee05aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383269} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c364af-a272-50a6-b30f-494f110bb9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383270} {:answer/id #uuid "243ec44e-50c3-5f68-80bc-c86f4f16c78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c364af-a272-50a6-b30f-494f110bb9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383270} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab6f04e5-e374-58d3-a929-8a7e744125e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7b651ee-2f62-5743-a764-86bdae6d7be2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80115" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,11,1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩=20.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩ & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,9⟩-⟨-2,11,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-7,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨2,-5,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
